## MCP Tool Knowledge Base

**Scope:** This file applies to ALL Cursor modes — Agent, Plan, Debug, and Ask.
It is not a code-creation-only reference. Any agent in any mode must consult
this file before deciding which tools to use. Ignoring these tools because you
are in Plan, Debug, or Ask mode is a rule violation.

**Purpose:** Persistent reference so agents do not re-derive tool usage from
scratch each conversation. Run the `generate-mcp-briefing` skill to refresh
this file when MCP servers or tools change.

---

## Tool Mode Map

### Agent mode — full execution

**Required workflow (must call in this order for every Ansible change):**
- `validate-playbook` (ansible-mcp) — syntax check before touching a playbook
- `ansible_lint` (ansible) — lint after every edit
- `list_tasks` (sysoperator) — preview task execution before running
- `project-run-playbook` (ansible-mcp) — run the playbook
- `ansible-test-idempotence` (ansible-mcp) — confirm no changes on second run

**Required pre-task (before writing any task or role):**
- `inventory-graph` (ansible-mcp) — understand host/group structure
- `inventory-find-host` (ansible-mcp) — resolve merged variables for target host
- `ade_environment_info` (ansible) — confirm installed collections and Ansible version
- `zen_of_ansible` (ansible) — consult design philosophy when making structural decisions

**Required when [condition applies]:**
- `ansible-gather-facts` (ansible-mcp) — required when writing tasks that read host state (packages, files, services, users, etc.)
- `validate-yaml` (ansible-mcp) — required when editing any raw YAML file that is not a playbook
- `ansible-capture-baseline` (ansible-mcp) — required before any task that modifies system state with drift risk
- `vault-view` (ansible-mcp) — required when the task involves vault-encrypted variables or files
- `galaxy-install` (ansible-mcp) — required when requirements files are added or changed
- `ansible_navigator` (ansible) — required when an execution environment (EE) is in scope; otherwise use `project-run-playbook`

**Call when [trigger]:**
- `inventory-parse` (ansible-mcp) — need full merged group_vars/host_vars and `inventory-find-host` is insufficient
- `inventory-diff` (ansible-mcp) — need to compare two inventory states before or after a change
- `ansible_inventory` (ansible-mcp) — need a raw host/group list; prefer `inventory-graph` for richer output
- `ansible-compare-states` (ansible-mcp) — need to diff current state against a previously captured baseline
- `ansible-role` (ansible-mcp) — testing a role in isolation before integrating into a playbook
- `galaxy-lock` (ansible-mcp) — pinning installed collection/role versions after a `galaxy-install`
- `vault-encrypt` / `vault-decrypt` (ansible-mcp) — encrypting or decrypting vault files as part of the task
- `vault_encrypt_string` / `vault_decrypt_string` (sysoperator) — encrypting/decrypting a single string value
- `project-playbooks` (ansible-mcp) — discovering what playbooks exist before deciding which to run
- `list-projects` (ansible-mcp) — confirming project registration before running
- `adt_check_env` (ansible) — verifying the dev environment state before running
- `ansible-playbook` (ansible-mcp) — running a playbook directly when project context is not needed; otherwise prefer `project-run-playbook`
- `ansible-task` (ansible-mcp) — running an ad-hoc module call during development; prefer a proper task in a role for anything repeatable
- `run_ad_hoc` (sysoperator) — fallback only when `ansible-task` from ansible-mcp is unavailable

**Not used in Agent mode unless task is explicitly about it:**
- `create_ansible_projects`, `define_and_build_execution_env` (ansible) — project scaffolding only
- `check_syntax` (sysoperator) — redundant with `validate-playbook`
- All AWS tools, `terraform` (sysoperator) — different domain
- All `cursor-ide-browser` tools — different domain
- `ansible-security-audit` (ansible-mcp) — security audit domain

