### Plan mode — read-only planning, no execution

**Plan mode pre-flight — numbered gate (complete ALL before producing any output):**

1. `inventory-graph` (ansible-mcp) — understand what hosts/groups are in scope
2. `inventory-find-host` (ansible-mcp) — resolve merged variables for any host referenced in plan
3. `ade_environment_info` (ansible) — verify collections are installed before recommending modules
4. `zen_of_ansible` (ansible) — consult before any structural or design recommendation
5. FetchMcpResource `guidelines://ansible-content-best-practices` (ansible) — fetch before answering any question about Ansible idiom, patterns, or best practice

**STOP — do not produce any plan output until steps 1–5 are complete.**

**Required when [condition applies]:**
- `list_tasks` (sysoperator) — REQUIRED for any existing playbook that will be added to **or modified**. Run before proposing any change to an existing playbook — not only when deciding where to add new tasks

**Call when [trigger]:**
- `ansible-gather-facts` (ansible-mcp) — live host state is required to make a recommendation in the plan
- `inventory-parse` (ansible-mcp) — full merged group_vars/host_vars is needed; `inventory-find-host` is insufficient
- `inventory-diff` (ansible-mcp) — comparing two inventory states as part of the plan
- `ansible_inventory` (ansible-mcp) — raw host/group list needed; prefer `inventory-graph` for richer output
- `list_inventory` (sysoperator) — fallback only when `inventory-graph` from ansible-mcp is unavailable

**Not used in Plan mode:**
- `validate-playbook`, `ansible_lint`, `project-run-playbook`, `ansible-test-idempotence` — nothing is executed until plan is approved and mode switches to Agent
- All destructive or write tools

