## Tools Not Covered in ansible-mcp-first.mdc or Other Existing Rules

The following tools exist in your MCP servers but are NOT mentioned in ansible-mcp-first.mdc.
They are documented in the mode map above but have no workflow in the curated rule file:

**ansible server:**
- `zen_of_ansible` — should be used for design decisions (not in ansible-mcp-first.mdc)
- `ansible-content-best-practices` resource — should be used for idiom questions (not in ansible-mcp-first.mdc)
- `ade_setup_environment` — environment setup (explicit request only)
- `define_and_build_execution_env` — EE build (explicit request only)
- `create_ansible_projects` — project scaffolding (explicit request only)
- `adt_check_env`, `list_available_tools` — env diagnostics (discretionary)
- `execution-environment-*` resources — EE reference docs (discretionary)

**ansible-mcp server:**
- `ansible_inventory` — list inventory hosts/groups; prefer inventory-graph for richer output (discretionary)
- `ansible-task` — run ad-hoc module; prefer ansible-remote-command for remote commands (discretionary)
- `inventory-diff` — compare inventory states (discretionary)
- `ansible-auto-heal` — automated healing (explicit request only)
- `ansible-performance-baseline` — performance baselining (discretionary)
- `project-bootstrap`, `register-project`, `list-projects` — project management (explicit request only)
- `create-playbook` — playbook scaffolding (explicit request only)
- `ansible-network-matrix` — connectivity matrix (discretionary in Debug)

**sysoperator server:**
- `terraform` and all `aws_*` tools — different domain entirely (explicit request only)
- `run_playbook` — use `project-run-playbook` from ansible-mcp instead; sysoperator version is a fallback

**cursor-ide-browser server:**
- All browser tools — web automation, separate domain entirely (explicit request only)
